  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Rohde and Schwarz Usa has $424M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date across 72 awards, with an average award size of $5.9M. Rohde and Schwarz Usa is up 235.7% year over year in obligations for the current fiscal-year-to-date period. Rohde and Schwarz Usa received substantially more obligations from the Department of Transportation than from other agencies, with $403M obligated by that agency. Rohde and Schwarz Usa earns most of its FY2026 to date revenue in the Telephone Apparatus Manufacturing market, which accounts for $403M of obligations. Historical obligations for Rohde and Schwarz Usa show a rising trend into FY25 and a larger jump in FY26, with prior fiscal-year totals of $20.2M in FY21, $25M in FY22, $56.2M in FY23, $35.3M in FY24, and $126M in FY25.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did obligations change in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Rohde and Schwarz Usa is up 235.7% year over year in FY2026 to date obligations. Rohde and Schwarz Usa has $424M in obligations this fiscal year compared with $126M in FY25. Rohde and Schwarz Usa shows a steep increase from the prior fiscal years, where obligations ranged from $20.2M to $126M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buyers and which markets dominate?",
        "body": "Department of Transportation is the top buyer of Rohde and Schwarz Usa with $403M in obligations for FY2026 to date. Department of Defense is the next largest buyer with $18.6M. Telephone Apparatus Manufacturing is the largest market for Rohde and Schwarz Usa at $403M, followed by Instrument Manufacturing for Measuring and Testing Electricity and Electrical Signals at $8.8M and Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $8.4M."
      }
    ]
